---
source: crates/wows-query/tests/game_data.rs
expression: output
---
group: tier 10 destroyers
ranked: 40
test: 4
torpedo_options: 43
reference_range_km: 10
factors:
  - "health (HP, higher is better): hit points"
  - "repair_party_heal (%, higher is better): share of maximum HP one Repair Party charge restores, stock"
  - "main_battery_reload (s, lower is better): main battery reload"
  - "main_battery_range (km, higher is better): main battery firing range"
  - "dpm_ap (HP/min, higher is better): main battery damage per minute of this ammo against one target at the bearing where the most of it bears, every shell hitting"
  - "dpm_he (HP/min, higher is better): main battery damage per minute of this ammo against one target at the bearing where the most of it bears, every shell hitting"
  - "dpm_sap (HP/min, higher is better): main battery damage per minute of this ammo against one target at the bearing where the most of it bears, every shell hitting"
  - "alpha_ap (HP, higher is better): damage of one salvo of every main battery barrel of this ammo"
  - "alpha_he (HP, higher is better): damage of one salvo of every main battery barrel of this ammo"
  - "alpha_sap (HP, higher is better): damage of one salvo of every main battery barrel of this ammo"
  - "flight_time_ap (s, lower is better): flight time of the largest main battery shell of this ammo to the reference range; absent when the range is beyond the ship's reach"
  - "flight_time_he (s, lower is better): flight time of the largest main battery shell of this ammo to the reference range; absent when the range is beyond the ship's reach"
  - "flight_time_sap (s, lower is better): flight time of the largest main battery shell of this ammo to the reference range; absent when the range is beyond the ship's reach"
  - "turret_traverse (s, lower is better): time a main battery turret takes to turn 180 deg"
  - "dispersion (m, lower is better): main battery horizontal dispersion at the reference range, or at the ship's own range when shorter"
  - "sigma (sigma, higher is better): main battery sigma; higher puts more shells near the aim point"
  - "fires_per_minute (fires/min, higher is better): fire starts per minute of every armament against one target at its best bearing, every projectile hitting"
  - "bow_barrels (%, higher is better): share of main battery barrels that bear on a target within 30 deg of the bow, at the best bearing"
  - "stern_barrels (%, higher is better): share of main battery barrels that bear on a target within 30 deg of the stern, at the best bearing; kiting"
  - "all_bear_from_bow (deg, lower is better): smallest angle off the bow at which every main battery barrel bears"
  - "all_bear_from_stern (deg, lower is better): smallest angle off the stern at which every main battery barrel bears; the kiting angle"
  - "secondary_dpm (HP/min, higher is better): secondary battery damage per minute, each group at its own best bearing, added up, every shell hitting"
  - "secondary_range (km, higher is better): secondary battery firing range"
  - "torpedo_dpm (HP/min, higher is better): torpedo damage per minute of the best torpedo against one target at its best bearing, every torpedo hitting"
  - "torpedoes_per_minute (torpedoes/min, higher is better): torpedoes launched per minute against one target at its best bearing, with the loaders' limit"
  - "torpedo_reload (s, lower is better): torpedo tube reload"
  - "torpedo_launch_from_bow (deg, lower is better): smallest angle off the bow at which a torpedo launcher bears; 0 launches bow-on"
  - "broadside_tubes (tubes, higher is better): torpedo tubes that bear on one broadside at once"
  - "aa_damage (HP/s, higher is better): continuous anti-aircraft damage per second of every aura, stock, before hit chance; flak bursts not counted"
  - "aa_range (km, higher is better): reach of the longest anti-aircraft aura, stock"
  - "concealment (km, lower is better): detectability by ships"
  - "air_concealment (km, lower is better): detectability by aircraft"
  - "speed (kn, higher is better): top speed"
  - "rudder_shift (s, lower is better): rudder shift time"
  - "turning_circle (m, lower is better): turning circle radius"
torpedo_factors:
  - "speed (kn, higher is better): torpedo speed"
  - "range (km, higher is better): torpedo range"
  - "damage (HP, higher is better): damage of one torpedo hit at full damage"
  - "damage_at_max_range (HP, higher is better): damage of one torpedo hit at the end of its run; less than damage for torpedoes whose damage falls with distance"
  - "flood_coefficient (x, higher is better): flooding coefficient of one hit (uwCritical), reduced by the target's torpedo protection; a relative weight, not a probability"
  - "detectability (km, lower is better): distance at which ships detect the torpedo"
  - "reaction_time (s, lower is better): time a target has from detecting the torpedo until it arrives: detectability / speed"
  - "damage_per_minute (HP/min, higher is better): torpedo damage per minute, every torpedo hitting"
